                        "entry_id": "4afa4607-e228-3422-8c1a-75ef5c81817a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The largest type of aircraft carrier, usually displacing over 70,000 long tons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2b34d73-40ce-41b3-894b-6b2b24145356",
                                "sense_id": "9aa196cf-8cb9-37ec-9b6f-f84bfd6cf35d",
                                "text": "Even the Navy has jumped back into the Osprey game with the decision to use a variant of the V-22 as a replacement for the aging C-2 Greyhound, a fixed-wing cargo plane used to ferry material and personnel on and off Navy supercarriers at sea. And other nations are now interested in procuring the V-22."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f866df30-128b-4f18-bb38-0ca0617bac80",
                                "sense_id": "9aa196cf-8cb9-37ec-9b6f-f84bfd6cf35d",
                                "text": "Sean J. Stackley, the Navy’s assistant secretary for acquisitions, gave the timetable for the 100,000-ton, 1,100-foot-long supercarrier in testimony prepared for the Senate Armed Services Committee on Wednesday."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c3c079d-6751-48f2-804f-bdba90d2578b",
                                "sense_id": "9aa196cf-8cb9-37ec-9b6f-f84bfd6cf35d",
                                "text": "Displacing around 80,000 metric tons of water, according to the China Daily report, the Fujian is 50% larger than China’s two current in-service carriers and puts the PLA Navy in the league of supercarriers, like the 100,000-ton US Nimitz-class ships."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
